  "releaseNotes": "v0.4.0: adds the ModelDisplayNames.ObjectDate label (Stored Date / Vistað dags., the time the provider stored the record) used by the DK Plus ObjectDate members, and the ModelDisplayNames SumReference, ReverseAccount, SubName, TaxType, InputTaxType, TaxAccount, InUse, Reconcile, PercentageOfVat and ValidTo labels (English and Icelandic) used by the DK Plus general-ledger create requests. v0.3.0 (breaking): portable models are now lean and unsealed. Customer, Product, Employee, Project, SalesPerson and the sales documents keep only members that another ERP clearly shares; DK Plus configuration, codes, enums, memos, change history and attachment metadata moved to DkPlus subtypes in DevOp.DK.Plus. Removes CustomerOptions, CustomerContactDetails, CustomerItemReceiver, CustomerProperty, MemoPage, EntityChange, FieldChange, AttachmentInfo, the product and project grouped detail models, and Project.RecordId (ErpEntity.ExternalId is the identity). Adds the portable Vendor model, IErpPurchaseResource (IExternalErpClient.Purchase.Vendor) with ErpCapability.Vendors, SalesDocumentParty, SalesDocument.Customer, AmountWithTax and ExchangeRate, and a lean SalesDocumentLine. Consumers that serialize or log by runtime type (ASP.NET Core output formatters, Serilog destructuring) emit provider subtype members; project results to your own DTOs.",
